// Title: Suspicious IIS Module Registration
// Sigma ID: 043c4b8b-3a54-4780-9682-081cb6b8185c
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems), Microsoft (idea)
// Date: 2022-08-04 | Modified: 2023-01-23
// ATT&CK: persistence, T1505.004
// Description: Detects a suspicious IIS module registration as described in Microsoft threat report on IIS
//   backdoors
// False positives:
//   - Administrative activity
// References:
//   - https://www.microsoft.com/security/blog/2022/07/26/malicious-iis-extensions-quietly-open-persistent-backdoors-into-servers/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_iis_susp_module_registration.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\w3wp.exe" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "appcmd.exe add module" or (ProcessCommandLine contains " system.enterpriseservices.internal.publish" and FolderPath endswith "\\powershell.exe") or (ProcessCommandLine contains "gacutil" and ProcessCommandLine contains " /I"))
